Ms. Du has also served as a Commissioner[ on the Nevada] Commission on Economic Development since 2008. She graduated[ from the] University[ of] California[-]Berkeley (Boalt Hall) in 1994, and[ from the] University[ of] California[-Davis] with Honors[ in] 1991.
Ms. Du left Vietnam with her family by boat when she was eight years old, and[ imm]igrated to Alabama after spending a year in refugee camps in Malaysia.
NAPABA[ and AA]JC[ join] in thanking President Obama for nominating Ms. Du and Senate Majority Leader Harry Reid for recommending her to the President.
